  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Two Independent Read/Writes",
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "One Decoder layer has an Attention and an FFN mHC boundary, each with separate hc_*_fn, hc_*_base, hc_*_scale.",
        "hc_pre reads four streams into one width-4096 input. The sublayer executes once, and hc_post writes its output into streams with distinct post coefficients.",
        "The old-stream update uses transpose(C) times R. Entry copies are equal; different post coefficients can make them differ, but need not always do so."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Logic and Fusion",
      "dot": "amber",
      "items": [
        "Post/pre are separated to show dependencies. The implementation may fuse Attention post with FFN pre while preserving both operations.",
        "Shapes denote complete logical widths; distributed partial outputs must satisfy the corresponding stage-boundary contract."
      ]
    }
  ]
